Usage:
  nucleus doctor [flags]

Run diagnostic checks for framework subsystems; exits non-zero when any check fails.

Checks (--check):
  tasks          Configured jobs provider; with asynq, queue reachability over Redis
  outbox         Outbox dispatcher and pending events
  storage        Storage backend configuration; a live probe only when targeted explicitly
  observability  OpenTelemetry exporters and metrics
  tenancy        Multi-tenant configuration and isolation
  rbac           RBAC policy file and enforcer
  security       High-risk misconfiguration: CORS, trusted proxies, signing key, CSRF
  auth           Authentication chain: backend order, per-backend configuration, break-glass path

Flags:
  -check string
    	Specific check to run (default: all)
  -config string
    	Path to nucleus config file
  -json
    	Output results as JSON
  -verbose
    	Show detailed output for each check

Examples:
  nucleus doctor --config nucleus.yml
  nucleus doctor --config nucleus.yml --check security
  nucleus doctor --config nucleus.yml --json
